WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.080
The school weekend combines advanced respiratory reading with complex cardiac and multisystem practice. This rehearsal brings those requirements together rather than replacing them with another unrelated chapter list.
学校本周把高级呼吸阅读与复杂心脏、多系统实操结合。本演练把要求连起来，不用另一个无关章节列表替代。

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:25.008
Use the earlier diagnostic, respiratory and twelve-lead sessions as working tools. Practise what you assess, say, do and reassess when new information appears.
应把此前诊断、呼吸及十二导联课当工作工具，练新信息出现时评什么、说什么、做什么及重评什么。

00:00:25.008 --> 00:00:37.320
The original cases here follow the school objectives without reproducing a school quiz or submitted response. Use a tabletop, training equipment or an observed classroom exercise as appropriate.
这里原创病例遵循学校目标，不复制学校测验或提交答案。可依条件桌面、训练器材或受观察课堂练习。

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:48.960
Treat immediate threats while explaining uncertainty. The purpose is executable clinical reasoning, not reciting a string of diagnosis names after the patient deteriorates.
应在处理即时威胁同时解释不确定。目的是可执行临床推理，不是患者恶化后背一串诊断。

00:00:48.960 --> 00:01:02.424
AP, FON and MSN explain gas transport and acid-base processes. Use them to describe a pattern and its limits, not to turn every low pH into one metabolic diagnosis.
AP、FON及MSN解释气体运输及酸碱过程。应用于描述模式和局限，不能把每个低pH都变一种代谢诊断。

00:01:02.424 --> 00:01:15.096
BCEHS and BCPEG supply separately identified procedure and examination wording. Keep different revisions, targets and eligibility decisions visible rather than averaging them.
BCEHS及BCPEG提供分别注明的规程和考试措辞。不同修订、目标及资格决定应明确，不取平均。

00:01:15.096 --> 00:01:27.984
CV and PHARM connect conduction, ischemia and medication risk; CNS links fluid/electrolyte assessment, respiratory support and infusion safety to the same patient.
CV及PHARM联系传导、缺血和药物风险，CNS把容量电解质评估、呼吸支持及输液安全连到同一患者。

00:01:27.984 --> 00:01:42.000
CPSC and VSM teach equipment and trustworthy observations; PMHN prevents diagnostic overshadowing. Nancy remains the main textbook bridge, not a substitute for those eleven assigned rows.
CPSC及VSM教设备与可信观察，PMHN防诊断遮蔽。Nancy仍作主教材桥接，不能替代十一项指定阅读。

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:51.792
Before class, explain the advanced ECG patterns without claiming new LBBB alone proves MI or every high-lateral event is an equivalent.
课前应能解释高级ECG模式，不称新LBBB单独证明梗死，也不说所有高侧壁都等价型。

00:01:51.792 --> 00:02:03.144
Reconstruct the complete CPAP and PEEP screens and stop plans. If the patient no longer meets the functional requirements, change support rather than defend the first choice.
需重建完整CPAP及PEEP筛查停止计划。患者不再符合功能要求时，应改支持，不维护最初选择。

00:02:03.144 --> 00:02:13.464
Explain why saturation, carbon dioxide and pressure describe different parts of the system. A good value in one part cannot guarantee the others are safe.
应解释饱和度、CO2及血压为何描述系统不同部分。一处数值好，不能保证其他都安全。

00:02:13.464 --> 00:02:23.712
Practise a complete alert with a timer, and practise a deterioration interrupting your plan. Do not rehearse only the version in which every treatment works.
要计时练完整预警，也练恶化打断计划。不能只练每种治疗都有效的版本。

00:02:23.712 --> 00:03:08.088
Apply the assigned counting technique to a suitable observation, not as a delay in an emergency. One breath is the entire inspiration-expiration cycle. In a regular resting pattern the source counts thirty seconds and doubles it; with an irregular rhythm it counts a full minute, and it uses a full minute for infants. Observe chest and abdominal movement, symmetry, depth, sounds and effort. Explain and document relevant crying, movement, pain or activity rather than calling that an unqualified resting value. In the weekly deteriorating patient, recognize ineffective breathing and support it immediately instead of finishing a routine count while the patient fails.
把指定计数技术用于合适观察，不能让它延误急救。一次呼吸是完整吸气加呼气；规则静息时来源数30秒乘二，不规则则数整分钟，婴儿也用整分钟。观察胸腹运动、对称、深度、声音及呼吸功；有哭闹、移动、疼痛或活动，应说明并记录，不能不加限定称静息数值。本周恶化患者中，应立即识别并支持无效呼吸，不能为了完成常规计数而看着患者衰竭。

00:03:08.088 --> 00:03:19.200
The team lead states the main threat and immediate priorities. Shared understanding is more useful than several providers independently pursuing their favorite diagnosis.
领队应说明主要威胁及即时优先级。共同理解比几人各追偏好诊断更有用。

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:27.528
Assign airway and breathing support explicitly so it does not disappear while an ECG is printed or an alert is delivered.
应明确分配气道呼吸支持，避免打印ECG或预警时照护消失。

00:03:27.528 --> 00:03:38.760
Assign circulation, hemorrhage and the usable ECG with clear feedback. Ask for the actual finding and time, not merely whether the task is done.
需分配循环、出血及有用ECG，并清楚反馈。要问真实发现时间，不只任务做完没有。

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:48.624
Use closed-loop communication for changes and requests. When a provider notices a discrepant trend, the team must hear and reassess it promptly.
变化和请求需闭环。有人发现矛盾趋势时，团队必须听到并及时重评。

00:03:48.624 --> 00:04:00.696
The primary threat is the problem most immediately endangering airway, breathing or circulation. It is not automatically the oldest diagnosis or the most dramatic ECG label.
主要威胁是最直接危及气道、呼吸或循环的问题，不自动是最老诊断或最戏剧化ECG名称。

00:04:00.696 --> 00:04:11.016
A complicating condition changes reserve or the safety of treatment. Chronic cardiac disease may complicate hemorrhage without making blood loss unimportant.
并发背景改变储备或治疗安全。慢性心病可使失血更复杂，但不能使出血变不重要。

00:04:11.016 --> 00:04:21.336
The cause of an incident is another question. A medical event might precede a collision, yet uncontrolled traumatic bleeding may be the immediate priority afterward.
事件原因又是另一问题。医学事件可能先于车祸，但之后未控创伤出血仍可成为即时优先。

00:04:21.336 --> 00:04:29.520
State each separately and update the priority when observations change. More than one problem can need parallel care.
应分别说明，观察变化后更新优先级。多个问题可以需要并行照护。

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:39.768
Before a planned intervention, state the working explanation and a dangerous alternative. The school wants this reasoning verbalized, not kept invisible.
计划干预前应说工作解释及危险鉴别。学校要求把推理说出来，不能只存在脑中。

00:04:39.768 --> 00:04:49.104
Choose an alternative that could change care, such as hemorrhage versus pump failure, pneumothorax versus edema or hypoventilation versus anxiety.
需选能改照护的鉴别，例如失血与泵衰、气胸与水肿、低通气与焦虑。

00:04:49.104 --> 00:04:59.016
Name a useful discriminator and the associated next action. A long unranked list that cannot change the plan is not a good differential check.
应说有用区分观察及相应下一行动。不能改计划的长而无排序列表，不是好的鉴别核查。

00:04:59.016 --> 00:05:10.032
Do not let the spoken check postpone immediate hemorrhage control, ventilation or arrest care. Parallel reasoning and rescue are safer than a ceremonial pause.
口头检查不能推迟即时止血、通气或骤停照护。并行推理救援，比仪式性暂停安全。

00:05:10.032 --> 00:05:20.328
First state what actually changed in breathing, mentation, perfusion or symptoms. A device setting change is not itself a patient response.
先说呼吸、意识、灌注或症状实际变什么。设备设定改变本身，不是患者反应。

00:05:20.328 --> 00:05:30.528
Next compare that observation with what the treatment should have changed and over what time. A slow anti-inflammatory effect should not be expected in seconds.
再与治疗应改变什么及何时改变相比。不能期待慢抗炎作用几秒奏效。

00:05:30.528 --> 00:05:41.736
Ask what worsened, including pressure after positive pressure or altered mentation despite improved saturation. An improved comfort goal can coexist with physiological harm.
需问什么更坏，包括正压后血压、或饱和度改善却意识变化。舒适目标改善，可以与生理伤害并存。

00:05:41.736 --> 00:05:52.464
Then make the next decision explicit: continue, adjust, stop or escalate. Reassessment only counts when the finding can influence care.
然后明确下一决定：继续、调整、停止或升级。发现能影响照护，才是有效复评。

00:05:52.464 --> 00:06:03.768
A sixty-six-year-old at a community repair workshop has been resuscitated by a trained team. Assume ROSC is confirmed and appropriate ongoing support is in place.
社区维修工作坊66岁者经受训团队复苏。假设已确认ROSC，且有适当持续支持。

00:06:03.768 --> 00:06:17.520
At the first reference point, ETCO2 is thirty-six, saturation ninety-seven percent and pressure one hundred four over sixty-eight. Record the actual airway and ventilation state with those values.
首参考点ETCO2为36、饱和度97%、血压104/68。应把真实气道通气状态与这些数一起记。

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:28.320
A single acceptable snapshot does not guarantee the next minute. Continue serial assessment and prepare the appropriate post-arrest ECG and conveyance pathway.
一次尚可切片，不保证下一分钟。应持续串联评估，准备适当骤停后ECG及转运路径。

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:38.880
Assign who watches the trend and who announces a change. The most important information may be the difference from this baseline, not a new isolated threshold.
需分配谁看趋势、谁通报变化。最重要信息可能是与这基线差异，而非新的孤立阈值。

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:51.216
Several minutes later ETCO2 falls to eighteen, saturation remains ninety-six and pressure is seventy-eight over forty-four. Responsiveness and perfusion also worsen.
几分钟后ETCO2降到18，饱和度仍96%，血压78/44，反应及灌注也变差。

00:06:51.216 --> 00:07:02.736
The acceptable oxygen percentage must not hide the circulatory threat. Reassess airway, effective breathing, pulse and the possibility of re-arrest promptly.
看似可接受氧百分比，不能遮住循环威胁。需迅速重评气道、有效呼吸、脉搏及再骤停可能。

00:07:02.736 --> 00:07:13.224
Check current support and the sampling circuit while necessary care continues. Treat the credible physiological deterioration rather than only troubleshooting a number.
必要照护持续时，核当前支持及取样回路。应处理可信生理恶化，不只是给数字排错。

00:07:13.224 --> 00:07:25.272
Do not reflexively ventilate faster because CO2 is low. If pulmonary blood flow has fallen, more ventilation can further impair the balance and miss the real problem.
不能CO2低就反射性吹更快。若肺血流下降，加通气可能更破坏平衡，并漏真实问题。

00:07:25.272 --> 00:07:37.296
ETCO2 depends on carbon-dioxide production, delivery to the lungs, effective ventilation and measurement. A sudden fall does not identify one mechanism by itself.
ETCO2依CO2产生、送到肺、有效通气及测量。突然下降，单独不能认定一个机制。

00:07:37.296 --> 00:07:48.048
Poor perfusion can reduce carbon dioxide reaching the lungs. In this case, falling pressure and responsiveness make that branch particularly urgent.
灌注差可减少送到肺的CO2。本例血压及反应下降，使该分支尤其紧急。

00:07:48.048 --> 00:08:01.680
Changes in ventilation or the airway/circuit can also lower the result. Inspect the waveform, chest movement, air entry, support settings and connections rather than assuming unchanged function.
通气或气道回路变化，也可降结果。应看波形、胸运动、进气、支持设定及连接，不能假定功能未变。

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:14.448
If arrest recurs, use the actual arrest pathway immediately. If a pulse remains, support the actual shock/respiratory problem and escalate without waiting for another gas.
若再骤停，应立即用真实骤停路径。若仍有脉，应支持真实休克呼吸问题并升级，不等下一血气。

00:08:14.448 --> 00:08:25.728
For the school Wednesday exercise, state its ninety-four-to-ninety-eight-percent target. Do not describe a saturation of one hundred as the goal simply because ROSC occurred.
学校周三练习应说其94%至98%目标。不能因已ROSC，就把100%说成目标。

00:08:25.728 --> 00:08:38.040
The checked N03 has different wording within its essentials and detailed interventions. Those differences are retained in the Week Five reading, not averaged into a new invented range.
核对N03在要点及详细干预中有不同措辞。差异已保留在第5周阅读，不平均成自创范围。

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:49.272
Correct immediate hypoxemia and use reliable monitoring to titrate through the actual pathway. Avoid unnecessary excessive oxygen without withholding needed treatment.
需纠正即时低氧，并用可靠监测依真实路径滴定。要避免不必要过量氧，但不扣住所需治疗。

00:08:49.272 --> 00:09:00.696
A target saturation cannot establish adequate ventilation, hemoglobin carriage or circulation. In Case A, a good percentage does not solve the falling pressure.
目标饱和度不能证明通气、血红蛋白携带或循环足够。本例百分比不错，也不能解决血压下降。

00:09:00.696 --> 00:09:12.840
Use appropriate effective ventilation and avoid excess rate or volume. An ETCO2 target assumes a valid measurement and enough pulmonary perfusion to interpret it.
应做适当有效通气，避免过快过量。ETCO2目标需有效测量及足够肺灌注，才可解释。

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:26.136
ETCO2 and arterial carbon dioxide are not always interchangeable, especially when perfusion or gas exchange changes. A field end-tidal number is not an arterial blood gas.
尤其灌注交换改变时，ETCO2与动脉CO2不总可互换。现场呼气末数不是动脉血气。

00:09:26.136 --> 00:09:39.624
Assess pressure and the broader perfusion picture. The checked N03 uses different pressure and carbon-dioxide wording in general versus advanced sections; keep the actual role-specific pathway explicit.
需评血压及更广灌注。核对N03一般与高级部分有不同血压及CO2措辞，应明确实际角色特定路径。

00:09:39.624 --> 00:09:50.760
Do not invent an automatic fluid or vasopressor order from a classroom target. Treat the likely mechanism, check response and coordinate the appropriate next capability.
不能从课堂目标自创自动补液或升压药医嘱。应处理可能机制、核反应并协调适当下一能力。

00:09:50.760 --> 00:10:01.560
Coordinate the post-ROSC ECG while continuing physiological support. Do not stop watching pressure and breathing because the team has reached an electrical task.
持续生理支持时协调ROSC后ECG。不能团队到了电任务，就不看血压呼吸。

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:16.632
Record acquisition timing relative to ROSC and important interventions. The saved school and current N03 timing language is not identical; use the named pathway rather than inventing a new combined clock.
要记相对ROSC及重要干预的采集时间。保存学校与现行N03时间措辞不全相同，需依具名路径，不能合成新时钟。

00:10:16.632 --> 00:10:28.392
Review the whole trace for ischemia and rhythm, including posterior clues, high lateral and conduction-related limitations. New LBBB alone is still not diagnostic.
应看全图缺血心律，包括后壁线索、高侧壁及传导局限。新LBBB单独仍不诊断。

00:10:28.392 --> 00:10:39.288
Communicate concerning findings and instability promptly. Do not wait for troponin or a perfectly certain culprit vessel before requesting the appropriate receiving capability.
应及时报可疑发现及不稳定。请求适当接收能力，不等肌钙蛋白或完全确定责任血管。

00:10:39.288 --> 00:10:51.024
Choose movement and conveyance through the actual pathway while continuing support. A transport plan must preserve access to the airway and the ability to respond to re-arrest.
应依真实路径移动转运并持续支持。转运计划必须保接近气道及再骤停响应能力。

00:10:51.024 --> 00:11:02.496
Check oxygen reserve, power, connections and monitoring before moving, then recheck afterward. Motion can disturb both treatment delivery and the apparent measurements.
移动前应核氧余量、电源、连接及监测，之后再核。运动可同时扰动治疗输送和表观测量。

00:11:02.496 --> 00:11:14.328
Secure lines without traction, keep required drainage orientation and have the appropriate backup ready. A neatly strapped patient can still have a disconnected respiratory circuit.
应固定管但无牵拉、保规定引流方向并备适当后备。患者绑整齐，呼吸回路仍可能已脱。

00:11:14.328 --> 00:11:23.184
Update the receiving team if support requirements or stability change. Give the current problem, not only the condition when the first alert was sent.
支持需要或稳定度变化时，应更新接收团队。需给当前问题，不只首预警时状态。

00:11:23.184 --> 00:11:34.848
A sixty-one-year-old driver is injured in a high-energy collision. A witness is unsure whether the driver became unwell before impact, and a cardiac history is reported.
61岁驾驶者高能量碰撞受伤。目击者不确定是否撞前先不适，且有人报告心病史。

00:11:34.848 --> 00:11:45.552
There is major external bleeding and poor perfusion now. Control the immediate traumatic threat while arranging appropriate airway, breathing and circulation care.
现在有大量外出血及灌注差。需控制即时创伤威胁，同时安排适当ABC。

00:11:45.552 --> 00:11:57.264
A cardiac event could have triggered the incident or coexist, but it does not explain away the blood loss. The cause of the crash and the present priority are distinct questions.
心脏事件可触发事故或并存，但不能搪塞失血。车祸原因与现在优先级，是不同问题。

00:11:57.264 --> 00:12:06.288
Use parallel team tasks to obtain relevant history and a useful ECG without delaying hemorrhage control or necessary conveyance.
应并行分工取相关病史及有用ECG，不能延误止血或必要转运。

00:12:06.288 --> 00:12:16.872
Use the established trauma approach, scene safety and appropriate resources. Do not narrow the encounter to an ECG because the patient has a cardiac history.
应依已学创伤流程、现场安全及适当资源。不能因心病史，就把接触缩成一张ECG。

00:12:16.872 --> 00:12:27.408
Control catastrophic bleeding and support airway, breathing and circulation. A spoken differential should happen alongside rescue, not postpone it.
需控灾难性出血并支持ABC。口头鉴别应与救援同时，不能推迟救援。

00:12:27.408 --> 00:12:39.096
Consider hidden hemorrhage, chest injury and other traumatic causes of shock through the actual indications and role. Positive pressure and medications can change risk in an injured patient.
应依真实指征角色考虑隐性出血、胸伤及其他创伤休克原因。正压和药物会改变伤者风险。

00:12:39.096 --> 00:12:50.664
Reassess the response and coordinate the receiving capability for the combined problem. Do not perform an unnecessary prolonged investigation to prove which event occurred first.
应复评反应并协调并存问题所需接收能力。不能为证明哪个事件先发生，做不必要漫长调查。

00:12:50.664 --> 00:13:01.368
Suppose a useful trace raises ischemic concern. Preserve and communicate it while continuing trauma care; neither evidence stream should erase the other.
假设有用图提示缺血。需保留沟通，同时继续创伤照护，两条证据不能互相抹掉。

00:13:01.368 --> 00:13:13.584
Before a cardiac medicine, check actual indications and exclusions, including active bleeding, pressure, volume status and the relevant interaction or consultation requirements.
心脏药前需核真实指征排除，包括活动出血、血压、容量及相关相互作用咨询要求。

00:13:13.584 --> 00:13:22.536
Do not reflexively give a nitrate to a poorly perfused bleeding patient or suppress compensatory tachycardia because the monitor rate is high.
不能反射性给低灌注出血者硝酸酯，也不能监护率高就压制代偿快率。

00:13:22.536 --> 00:13:33.648
State what is immediately primary, what is complicating and what remains uncertain. Coordinate the actual combined destination and escalation pathway.
应说当前主要、并发背景及未知，并协调真实并存问题目的地及升级路径。

00:13:33.648 --> 00:13:42.792
Ask brief questions that can change care, including symptom timing, collapse before impact, medications and relevant baseline function.
应问可改照护的简短问题，包括症状时间、是否撞前倒、药物及相关基线功能。

00:13:42.792 --> 00:13:54.408
Use witnesses, records or device information when available, but identify the source. A family report and a measured observation are not the same kind of evidence.
可用时使用目击、记录或设备信息，但要注明来源。家人报告与测量观察，不是同类证据。

00:13:54.408 --> 00:14:04.920
State uncertainty accurately: unknown anticoagulant use is not no anticoagulant, and no prior ECG is not a definitely new bundle block.
应准确说明未知。未知抗凝使用不等于没用，无旧ECG也不等于确定新束支阻滞。

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:15.720
Do not search belongings or pursue a complete history while immediate threats remain unsupported. Hand over what is missing so the next team can continue the investigation.
不能即时威胁无人支持时，还翻物或追完整病史。需交接缺什么，让下一团队继续查。

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:25.776
A patient may be anxious because breathing or circulation is failing. Respectful engagement is useful, but it is not proof that the cause is psychological.
患者可因呼吸循环失败而焦虑。尊重沟通有用，但不能证明病因为心理。

00:14:25.776 --> 00:14:37.368
New altered mentation requires the current medical assessment, including relevant oxygenation, ventilation, glucose, perfusion and medicine/substance context.
新意识改变需当前医学评估，包括相关氧合、通气、血糖、灌注及药物物质背景。

00:14:37.368 --> 00:14:48.624
Use the assigned PMHN framework to separate observation from diagnosis and avoid overshadowing. DSM classification does not replace urgent physical care.
应以指定PMHN框架区分观察诊断、防遮蔽。DSM分类不能替代紧急躯体照护。

00:14:48.624 --> 00:15:01.176
Calmer, cooperative or refusing are descriptions, not automatic statements about stability or decision-making capacity. Assess those questions through the actual clinical and legal process.
更平静、合作或拒绝，是描述，不自动说明稳定或决定能力。需依真实临床法律流程评这些问题。

00:15:01.176 --> 00:15:50.352
Keep the named U.S. organizations attached to their textbook functions. ANA develops general professional nursing standards; APNA and ISPN address psychiatric-mental-health nursing standards. NCSBN brings nursing regulators together, while the actual jurisdictional board enforces its Nurse Practice Act and makes licensure or disciplinary decisions. NLN emphasizes nursing education; AACN develops education competencies, and CCNE, ACEN and CNEA are named accreditation bodies. A professional association, school accreditor, employer and statutory regulator are not interchangeable. These names help you understand the assigned reading, not identify the authority governing a BC paramedic.
把点名的美国机构与教材中的职能对应：ANA制定一般专业护理标准，APNA及ISPN涉及精神健康护理标准；NCSBN联结护理监管机构，而实际辖区委员会执行其Nurse Practice Act并作执照或纪律决定。NLN侧重护理教育；AACN制定教育能力要求，CCNE、ACEN及CNEA是点名认证机构。专业协会、学校认证者、雇主及法定监管者不能互换。这些名称用于理解指定阅读，不用于认定BC急救人员的监管权限。

00:15:50.352 --> 00:16:36.960
Match the six nursing-process terms to the six CJMM steps: assessment to recognizing cues; diagnosis to analyzing cues; outcomes identification to prioritizing hypotheses; planning to generating solutions; implementation to taking action; evaluation to evaluating outcomes. This is the source table's comparison, not a rule that every real decision fits one box. Coordination of care and health teaching sit within implementation. In an original breathlessness rehearsal, collect the changing effort and pressure, compare explanations, prioritize the immediate threat, plan support, act and check the response; restart the cycle when observations disagree.
把六个护理流程词与六个CJMM步骤对应：评估对应识别线索，诊断对应分析线索，结果识别对应排列假设，计划对应形成方案，实施对应行动，评价对应评价结果。这是来源表的对照，不是现实每项决定都只能放一格的规则；协调照护及健康教育属于实施内容。原创气促演练中，收集变化呼吸功和血压、比较解释、优先处理即时威胁、计划支持、行动并查反应；观察不符就重新循环。

00:16:36.960 --> 00:17:30.432
Recall the six QSEN areas with their practical meaning: person-centered care hears the person's goals; teamwork shares a discrepant finding; evidence-based practice checks a claim; quality improvement examines a repeatable failure; safety prevents avoidable harm; informatics preserves reliable information. The reading also names HHS for broad U.S. health programs, CMS for Medicare/Medicaid administration, Healthy People 2030 for population goals, OSHA for worker safety and the Joint Commission for organizational quality accreditation. Its patient-safety examples include two identifiers, handover, medication checks, infection prevention, falls and alarm safety. They are source-context examples, not a current BC rulebook or a claim that a historical annual goal list is still unchanged.
用实际意义记六个QSEN领域：以人为中心要听本人目标，团队协作要分享矛盾发现，循证要核查主张，质量改进要检查可重复失误，安全要避免可防伤害，信息学要保存可靠信息。阅读还点名HHS负责广泛美国健康项目、CMS管理Medicare及Medicaid、Healthy People 2030提出人群目标、OSHA涉及劳动者安全，Joint Commission涉及机构质量认证。其患者安全例子包括双身份标识、交接、用药核对、感染预防、跌倒及警报安全；这些是来源背景，不是现行BC规则集，也不声称某历史年度目标表至今没变。

00:17:30.432 --> 00:18:17.856
Read the DSM structure as a reference framework: introductory purpose and limits, diagnostic criteria grouped by related disorders, assessment measures and models, cultural context, and supporting appendices or codes. A criterion set is more than a category name: the actual required symptoms, duration, impairment and exclusions must be checked by an appropriately trained clinician. This assigned chapter explains the framework and gives selected categories; it does not print every disorder's complete diagnostic criteria. Recognizing panic-like symptoms in a scenario therefore does not justify inventing a criterion checklist or dismissing hypoxemia, ischemia, intoxication or another concurrent cause.
把DSM结构当参考框架：导言说明目的和限制，按相关障碍分组的诊断标准，评估工具及模型，文化背景，以及支持附录或编码。标准组合不只是类别名，真实要求的症状、时间、功能影响及排除须由适当受训人员核查。指定章解释框架并列部分类别，并未印每种障碍全部诊断标准；所以情境中认识类似惊恐症状，不代表可自编标准清单或忽视低氧、缺血、中毒及其他并存病因。

00:18:17.856 --> 00:19:03.288
At the literal page ending, older adults may present differently and need an individualized baseline. Bereavement, mobility loss, isolation, cognitive change, mood, sleep, appetite and substance or medication history can matter; age alone proves none of them. New inattention or confusion during breathlessness needs assessment for acute medical causes rather than automatic attribution to dementia or depression. Preserve the patient's own report, observed changes, communication needs and collateral history, then hand over what is known and uncertain. The assigned page ends while this life-stage discussion continues; no unseen continuation is claimed read here.
实际指定末页提示，老年人表现可不同，需要个体基线。丧亲、活动受限、孤立、认知变化、心境、睡眠、食欲及物质或用药史都可能重要，但年龄本身不证明任一情况。气促中新注意力差或混乱，要评估急性医学原因，不能自动归为痴呆或抑郁。保留本人报告、观察变化、沟通需要及旁证病史，再交接已知和不确定。指定页在这一生命阶段讨论仍继续时结束，不声称读过不可见的后续指定内容。

00:19:03.288 --> 00:19:59.760
The wound-care literal ending teaches skin-edge support, patient education, hand hygiene and documentation after removal. Explain gentle cleaning and drying, protection from strain and recognition of separation, redness, swelling, discharge or other concerning changes. The source expects adhesive strips to loosen naturally and gives one-to-three weeks as an example, not a universal product-removal deadline. Advice about fluid intake, activity and bathing must fit the actual wound instructions and cardiac/renal restrictions. The next checklist begins continuous/blanket stitch removal with identity, consent, healing-risk/PPE checks and a valid order; this assigned page does not contain the remaining removal sequence. Do not promise a painless procedure or imply independent PCP suture-removal authority.
实际伤口页段末尾教授拆线后的皮缘支持、患者教育、手卫生及记录。应解释轻柔清洁擦干、避免牵张，并识别分开、红肿、渗出或其他可疑变化。来源期待胶条自然松脱，并举一至三周，不是所有产品统一移除期限；饮水、活动及沐浴建议还须符合真实伤口指示和心肾限制。下一清单的连续或毯式缝线拆除，只在指定页开始身份、同意、愈合风险、防护及有效医嘱核对，并未列出后续完整拆除过程；不能保证不痛，也不暗示PCP可独立拆线。

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:49.752
An implanted venous port has a reservoir beneath the skin joined to a catheter; it is not simply a visible peripheral cannula. Access uses the correct non-coring needle and specifically trained staff. Confirm the actual device, intended route, access status, reason and insertion history; the source also mentions devices terminating outside the vascular system, so a port-shaped object alone does not establish an IV route. Check dressing, securement, pain/redness/swelling, connected cap and tubing, each infusate, fever and respiratory/circulatory signs. This supports safe observation and handover, not puncturing an unfamiliar port or starting central-line therapy after reading a paragraph.
植入式静脉港是皮下储液座连接导管，不只是可见的外周留置针。接入需要正确无损伤针及特定受训人员；应确认真实装置、预期途径、是否已接入、原因及植入史。来源也提到终止于血管系统外的装置，因此看起来像港，不证明就是静脉途径。检查敷料、固定、疼痛红肿、连接帽和管路、每种输液、发热及呼吸循环表现。这支持安全观察和交接，不代表读完一段就可穿刺不熟悉的港或开始中心静脉治疗。

00:20:49.752 --> 00:21:34.776
A multilumen catheter contains separate internal paths with different exit locations. Trace each labelled external line to its actual lumen and prescribed infusate; assess each lumen separately. Separation inside the catheter is not proof that every drug pair, connector or shared segment is compatible. The source explanation of dilution in blood does not replace a real compatibility check. During the weekly transfer, a secure-looking triple-lumen line may still have one disconnected, clamped or wrongly connected branch. Protect the existing system, avoid traction and report the affected path rather than assuming the whole catheter is working because another channel flows.
多腔导管有独立内部通路和不同出口位置。应把每条已标外部管追到真实腔道及规定输液，分别评估各腔；导管内分开，不证明所有药物组合、接头或共用管段都相容，来源所说在血中稀释不能替代真实相容核查。本周转移时，看起来固定牢的三腔管，仍可有一支脱开、夹住或接错；应保护既有系统、防牵拉，报告受影响的通路，不能因另一腔有流就假设整管正常。

00:21:34.776 --> 00:22:23.760
The source contrasts an open distal tip with a pressure-activated valved design: in the illustrated valve, neutral pressure closes it, aspiration opens it inward and infusion pressure opens it outward. It associates open-ended devices with clamp and lock requirements and a low-dose heparin example, while its valved example needs no clamp. These are design examples, not universal instructions for every catheter, connector or implanted port. Confirm the manufacturer and agency-specific clamp/flush/lock sequence and solution before touching the system; do not add heparin, omit a required clamp or force a resistant flush from this comparison table alone. An untrained operator should protect and escalate a compromised line.
来源比较开放远端与压力激活带阀设计：所画阀在中性压力关闭，抽吸时向内开，输注压力时向外开。它把开放式与夹闭、封管要求及低剂量肝素例子联系，并称其带阀例子无需夹子；这些是设计例子，不是所有导管、接头或植入港的通用操作。接触系统前须核厂家和机构特定的夹闭、冲管、封管顺序及溶液，不能只凭比较表就加肝素、漏掉必要夹闭或强冲阻力通路；未受训者应保护受损管路并升级求助。

00:22:23.760 --> 00:22:34.656
Before moving, trace each relevant line and identify what it delivers or drains. Plan oxygen supply and airway access for the actual move.
移动前应追每条相关管，认输送或引流什么，并为实际移动计划氧源及气道接近。

00:22:34.656 --> 00:22:45.744
Assign responsibility for devices and avoid traction, kinks or unnecessary disconnection. The patient is not safely moved merely because the stretcher is locked.
需分配设备责任，防牵拉折曲及不必要断开。担架锁住，不代表患者已安全移动。

00:22:45.744 --> 00:22:56.952
Afterward repeat the primary observations and validate monitor signals. A new poor number may be artifact, but it may also be the first evidence of a real change.
之后需重复主要观察并核监护信号。新差数字可能伪差，也可能是真变化首证据。

00:22:56.952 --> 00:23:07.008
Treat credible threats while troubleshooting and record the fault, correction and clinical response. Do not hide the event by deleting an inconvenient reading.
应在排错时处理可信威胁，记故障、修正及临床反应，不能删不方便读数来藏事件。

00:23:07.008 --> 00:23:16.584
Use the school sixty-second target for a complete message, not a rushed inventory. Lead with the patient and immediate combined threat.
学校六十秒目标是完整信息，不是赶着报库存。应先患者及即时并存威胁。

00:23:16.584 --> 00:23:26.664
Give the important mechanism, symptom timing, current physiology and interpretable ECG concern. Distinguish a witness report from a confirmed cause.
需给重要机制、症状时间、当前生理及可解释ECG担忧，并区分目击报告和已证实原因。

00:23:26.664 --> 00:23:36.216
Report treatment actually provided and the response, including continuing deterioration. Do not imply a drug was given because it was considered.
应报实际治疗及反应，包括持续恶化。不能因考虑过，就暗示已给药。

00:23:36.216 --> 00:23:45.912
State ETA and the capability needed, then confirm the receiving plan. Keep the detailed chronology available for the fuller handover.
要给到达时间及所需能力，再确认接收计划。详细顺序留待更完整交接。

00:23:45.912 --> 00:23:58.512
Receiving team, training unit Alpha with a sixty-one-year-old driver after a high-energy collision. We have controlled major external bleeding, but the patient remains poorly perfused.
接收团队，训练Alpha单位，61岁驾驶者高能量碰撞后。大量外出血已控制，但患者仍低灌注。

00:23:58.512 --> 00:24:13.296
Current pressure is eighty-six over fifty, pulse one hundred twenty and saturation ninety-five on supplemental oxygen. A useful twelve-lead raises lateral ischemic concern; the pre-impact history remains uncertain.
当前血压86/50、脉120，补氧下饱和度95%。有用十二导联提示侧壁缺血担忧，撞前病史仍不确定。

00:24:13.296 --> 00:24:25.992
Airway and ventilation are being supported as indicated, with repeated primary assessment. We are continuing hemorrhage and perfusion care without assuming that the ECG explains all shock.
正按需要支持气道通气，并反复主要评估。我们持续出血灌注照护，不假定ECG解释全部休克。

00:24:25.992 --> 00:24:38.952
Estimated arrival is six minutes. We request the appropriate trauma capability with urgent cardiac review. Please confirm the receiving plan; we will update you immediately if support needs change.
预计六分钟到。请求适当创伤能力及紧急心脏评估，请确认接收计划；支持需要改变时，我们会立即更新。

00:24:38.952 --> 00:24:48.648
Record actual times for symptoms, ROSC, observations and treatment rather than reconstructing a neat but fictional sequence later.
应记录真实症状、ROSC、观察及治疗时间，不能后来重建整齐却虚构顺序。

00:24:48.648 --> 00:25:01.824
Preserve ECGs, sampling context and monitoring limitations. A venous oxygen number or poor waveform must not become an unquestioned arterial or reliable result in handover.
需保ECG、取样背景及监测局限。静脉氧值或差波形，不能交接时变成无疑动脉或可靠结果。

00:25:01.824 --> 00:25:11.112
Document the working explanation, dangerous alternative, important consultation and why a treatment was withheld, stopped or changed.
应记工作解释、危险鉴别、重要咨询，以及为何未给、停止或改变治疗。

00:25:11.112 --> 00:25:22.056
Finish with the patient response, current support and transfer of responsibility. Do not mark an unseen device checkoff or unperformed school skill as completed.
最后记患者反应、当前支持及责任转交。未见设备考核或未做学校技能，不能标完成。

00:25:22.056 --> 00:25:33.072
Reconstruct the actual timeline using observations and records. Separate a technical setup success from a clinical response and from observed hands-on competence.
应以观察记录重建真实时间线，分开技术设定成功、临床反应及受观察实体能力。

00:25:33.072 --> 00:25:44.256
Identify where the team anchored, lost a monitoring task or failed to hear a change. Include system and communication contributors rather than blaming the patient.
需找锚定、监测任务丢失或未听到变化之处，包括系统沟通因素，而非责患者。

00:25:44.256 --> 00:25:55.896
Select one measurable improvement, such as an earlier trend callout or a more complete sixty-second alert. A faster message is not an improvement if it omits the main threat.
选一项可测改进，如更早报趋势或更完整六十秒预警。若省主要威胁，报更快不算改进。

00:25:55.896 --> 00:26:06.144
Retest the changed process with a new variation. Actual compression, device fit and procedural competence still need the school observer and real training equipment.
应以新变体重测改变流程。真实按压、设备适配及操作能力，仍需学校观察者及真实训练设备。

00:26:06.144 --> 00:26:16.080
You should now connect reliable diagnostics, acid-base patterns, respiratory support and advanced ECG concern to one changing patient.
现在应能把可靠诊断、酸碱模式、呼吸支持及高级ECG担忧，连到一位变化患者。

00:26:16.080 --> 00:26:25.944
Explain the primary versus complicating problem, verbalize a useful What Else and evaluate what changed, what should change and what got worse.
应解释主要与并发问题，口述有用What Else，并评价什么变了、应怎样变及什么更糟。

00:26:25.944 --> 00:26:37.008
Practise the original CO2-fall and medical-trauma sequences with the bilingual reading, then deliver an accurate timed alert without abandoning primary care.
要结合中英阅读练原创CO2下降及医学创伤序列，再在不放弃主要照护下，做准确限时预警。

00:26:37.008 --> 00:26:50.928
The remaining source gaps are explicitly recorded, including original school slides and device rubrics. The next week follows the school medical-neurological, endocrine, sepsis and gastrointestinal requirements.
余下来源缺口已明确记录，包括学校原幻灯及设备评分表。下一周将依学校神经、内分泌、脓毒症及胃肠医学要求。
